<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Minbu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Minbu is a town on the west bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irrawaddy-river">Irrawaddy River</a> in central Myanmar, opposite Magway. Its district, watered by irrigation canals fed from the hill streams, was with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyaukse">Kyaukse</a> one of the two great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> granaries of the dry zone that supported the kingdoms of Pagan, Ava, Toungoo and Konbaung.</p></div>
